#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-infer — the perms seat's decider: is this ask one the box may grant itself, and does the owner's intent cover it?

  cc-infer decide --json FILE|- [--record]   one ask in, one verdict out (stdout: one JSON line)
  cc-infer decide --ask TEXT [--record]      the same for a bare command with no evidence (so never a grant)
  cc-infer digest [--hours N]                the told-after lines for the owner's daily digest (cc-reconcile digest)
  cc-infer backtest FILE                     replay past asks; exit 1 if one the owner refused, perms refused or the
                                             record keeps for him (owner-only) comes out a GRANT
  cc-infer selfcheck

The perms seat calls it, and so does the approver (`cc-approve decide …` runs this). It returns GRANT, GRANT+WATCH,
ASK-OWNER or REFUSE with its reasons and evidence; exit 0 on a GRANT or GRANT+WATCH, 1 otherwise, 2 on usage. ASK-OWNER
means the box doesn't grant it itself, and its `who` says who decides: "owner" for a hard line (rule 3), unreadable
letters or a claim that it reaches past him, "perms" for the rest, which perms decides for him. It fails closed: anything it can't read, parse or
resolve is not a grant.

A GRANT comes only from a closed set of command shapes, parsed from the ask's whole text, never matched against prose
(architect, 10-11: "An ask that doesn't parse to one of those shapes goes to perms (ASK) whatever its wording, kind or
evidence. Free text never reaches GRANT."). The shapes, and nothing else:

  cc-config set KEY N                  KEY one of CONFIG_KEYS below, N a whole number in that key's range with no
                                       leading zero: how much one cc-ask spends and waits (the same bounds as
                                       cc-approve's KEY_OK). Nothing that lands, reviews, sets the tier, routes, pages, or touches the guard, the sandbox
                                       or perms. Undo: KEY back to its value before (`cc-config set KEY OLD`, or
                                       `cc-config unset KEY` if it had none). When the old value can't be read, the
                                       caller's own undo stands only if it parses as this shape; else no runnable
                                       undo is recorded, only a note saying why (a watcher runs the undo unattended).
  systemctl --user restart cc-NAME     restart one of the box's own user units. Restart only: stop, disable and mask
                                       are hard lines. Undo: none to run; the unit runs as before. Only for a unit
                                       `systemctl --user is-active` reads as active now: a restart starts an inactive
                                       one, and its undo would be a stop, a hard line, so that (or a state it can't
                                       read) goes to perms.

Rules, deterministic and in this order, so the backtest replays them exactly:

  1. REFUSE an empty ask, one the record shows the owner already said no to (`owner_refused`), and port 22 anywhere
     in it: that is SSH into the host.
  2. ASK-OWNER when the text still holds non-Latin letters after folding (NFKC, zero-width marks dropped, look-alike
     Cyrillic and Greek letters mapped to Latin, accents stripped), so the rules can't read it.
  3. ASK-OWNER for the hard lines, whatever a goal says: real money; secrets and credentials; the never-touch list;
     unplanned deletion of shared state; widening a member or any non-owner; mail, posts or anything outward; opening
     the HOST (SSH, any port, a connector or tunnel into a shell); the box's own controls, perms' standing condition
     (perms' CLAUDE.md or settings, ~/.cc/approvals, hooks, the guard, the sandbox or bwrap, autoMode, the tier, a
     shell profile, ~/bin, tmux or cc-msg into a seat, any cc-config key off the list); code fetched or decoded from
     outside the box; docker or any container run; a cron-style or every-N schedule; stopping or disabling a daemon;
     a push or merge (its target can't be read off prose, and a bare push goes to the default branch); and reading,
     writing or copying ~/.cc/config or ~/.cc/env. The folded text is matched whatever the `kind` says, and a hard
     kind is enough alone. Each reason names the word or kind that matched. Not matched, here or for the ports of rule
     1: a negated clause of plain words that ends with its clause ("no secrets, no member widening"), a Z-stamped or
     dated time ("03:21Z"), and a ref ending in a default branch ("origin/main"); a verb beside them still matches. These are an extra refusal layer: rule 4
     is what keeps a rewording out.
     One carve-out, read before the hard lines (owner, 10-12, above credential_move()): an ask whose text names a
     credential and copies it where its readers widen (a member or workspace, a member's name from ~/.cc/members,
     anything public, an env name a site ships to its client code like VITE_ or PUBLIC_, a log, a commit, Slack, or a
     `reaches` past the owner) is REFUSE. One that moves or copies a credential the box already holds into its own
     services (an env, cc-config, a unit, Pages or Workers), where every place it copies into names one, no path
     appears, no word of minting or rotating appears (env names included), and every other hard line it crosses
     matches only on the word cc-config, is ASK-OWNER with who "perms": perms' call, never a grant.
  4. ASK-OWNER unless the whole ask parses to one of the shapes above.
  5. ASK-OWNER with no resolved evidence of his intent that shares a content word with the ask: no evidence, no grant.
  6. `reaches` and `reversible` are claims, and only a stricter one counts: a claim past the owner, or that it can't
     be undone, is ASK-OWNER. GRANT when it undoes in minutes; GRANT+WATCH, with the shape's undo, when it claims hours.

Owner, 10-11: the perms seat must infer low-level permissions from his high-level goals and weigh each against its
actual risk, "because many things can be reverted". His example was a client's test site, which waited on his yes to
go public though his wish for it was in Slack and its subdomain was already planned. A public site has no parsed shape
here yet, so it goes to perms.

THE ASK (JSON). `ask` is required, and is the command itself; every other key is optional.
  kind        a claim; mail|post|money|secret|never-touch|delete-shared|widen-member|open-host|controls keep it with the
              owner on their own, and any other value changes nothing (the shape is what decides)
  reaches     box|owner|member|public|outside-person   only a value past the owner counts
  reversible  minutes|hours|no                         hours makes a grant watched; no keeps it with the owner
  money       true keeps it with the owner;  data  secret keeps it with the owner
  evidence    [{"quote": "...", "source": "..."}]. A quote counts when it is at least 20 characters (or is a whole go
              template, below, cited from Slack or goals.md), shares a content word with the ask (not a stopword, a
              shape's own word or a repo name), and is found for real in one line of one of these, a heading or a
              line under 20 characters counting only for such a template:
                ~/.cc/state/<repo>/goals.md, where <repo> is one of the owner's own repos (CC_JANITOR_REPOS in his
                ~/.cc/config, read through cc-config with HOME, CC_CONFIG and CC_CONFIG_DENY pinned) and not a member
                workspace (~/.cc/members/<repo> without its owner-workspace marker); never a goals.md under ~/dev/
                or anywhere else;
                grant:N, item N of the owner's one-time grant in docs/host-rules.md;
                slack:<channel>/<ts>, one Slack message of his (below).
              A goals.md line counts only when it carries its own `src: slack:<channel>/<ts>` and that source holds
              for the same quote; a line with no src: steers the seat's own work but grants nothing (design 10-12,
              docs/architecture/goals-first-approvals.md: goals.md is an index, not an authority). His 👍 on the commit that
              added a line, the design's other route, is a deliberate follow-up and not read here. A Slack source is
              fetched from Slack with the bot token when it is checked, never read from a file: conversations.history
              for a top-level message, conversations.replies for a thread reply. It holds when the message is there
              now, its user is SLACK_OWNER_ID with no bot_id, it is a message he wrote (no subtype but
              thread_broadcast or file_share, so never a channel_topic or join line), the quote names the ask's own
              key, every word of it whole (CC_ASK_TURNS: "ask" and "turns"), or the unit's whole name (cc-slackd, never
              cc-slackd-old, nor a path like ~/cc-slackd/x), and the quote is his WHOLE message in its current text
              (only a final . or ! may drop), after any edit, with his markup read as its words: one line, one
              sentence, no code, mention, struck text or question, that is exactly one go template for the ask, with nothing after it: "set <key words> to
              N" or "give <key words> N <noun>" (Set cc-ask turns to 16, Give cc-ask 16 turns; N the value the ask
              sets) or "restart <unit>" (Restart cc-watchdog). Anything else, "Give cc-ask 16 more turns", "Raise
              cc-ask turns by 16" or "Give cc-ask 16 turns next week", is perms'. It fails closed on his meaning (#1129): a message in which any
              negation, condition, retraction, rejection or reported-speech word stands anywhere (not, never, no, n't,
              unless, until, only, but, wait, hold, if, maybe, kidding, ignore, rejected, asked, said, wants, …), or a sentence opens
              like a question (should, can, would, what, …) with no ?, grants nothing, so "Never …", "If Bob
              agrees, …", "Bob asked me this today." or "Just kidding." never reads as a go. The grant keeps his whole message.
              ~/.cc/state/owner-words.jsonl, the owner's words as cc-slack records them, is only a cache any session
              could write, so a line in it grants nothing; it is read for one thing, a deletion, which revokes every
              goal citing that message.
              A cc-lib ticket is no evidence: tickets.log records no message, so its quote can't be tied to what it
              answered. ~ is the account's home from the password database, never $HOME, and only selfcheck() swaps
              these places, and the ledger's, for scratch ones, so the caller can't choose the evidence.
  owner_refused  where the record shows he refused it;  check  how a watcher sees it is fine (the undo is the shape's, above)

--record writes, for a GRANT or GRANT+WATCH only: one line in the ledger (~/.cc/state/perms/inferred.jsonl: what,
evidence, watcher, revert, revert_note) and, for GRANT+WATCH, a watcher registration in ~/.cc/state/perms/watch-spool/<id>.json. The watcher framework (row perms-grant-watchers) has not landed, so the spool is the interface until it does:
one JSON object per file with id, created, what, check, revert, revert_note, expires and evidence. revert is a
command a watcher may run, or "" when there is none, and then revert_note says why. The owner sees the ledger in the
11:00 digest as told-after, never as a card, with the ask text escaped so it can't ping or link in Slack.
"""
import json, os, pwd, re, shlex, subprocess, sys, time, unicodedata

# the account's own home, never $HOME: the caller must not choose where evidence is read from (security read, 10-11)
HOME = pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir
USAGE = "usage: cc-infer decide (--json FILE|- | --ask TEXT) [--record] | digest [--hours N] | backtest FILE | selfcheck"
GRANTS = ("GRANT", "GRANT+WATCH")
WATCH_DAYS = 7


# Stand-ins for the places evidence, the owner's repos and the ledger come from. Only selfcheck() sets them; a normal
# run reads no environment for them, so whoever runs the tool can't choose its evidence (security read, 10-11: "CC_INFER_*
# path overrides take effect only inside selfcheck(); in a normal run they're ignored").
_TEST = {}


def place(key, default):
    return _TEST[key] if key in _TEST else default


def state_dir():
    return place("dir", f"{HOME}/.cc/state/perms")


# The closed set of command shapes (architect, 10-11: "GRANT comes only from a closed, enumerated set of command
# shapes, parsed, not pattern-matched against prose"). cc-config keys: how much one cc-ask spends and waits, held in
# the ranges cc-approve's KEY_OK holds them in. A key joins by a reviewed PR, never by an ask.
CONFIG_KEYS = {"CC_ASK_TURNS": (1, 24), "CC_ASK_TIMEOUT": (30, 300), "CC_ASK_THINK": (0, 10000),
               "CC_ASK_PACKET": (1024, 16384)}
SHAPES = [("config", re.compile(r"cc-config set (" + "|".join(CONFIG_KEYS) + r") (0|[1-9]\d{0,5})")),
          ("service", re.compile(r"systemctl --user restart (cc-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*)(?:\.service)?"))]
SHAPE_WORDS = {"cc", "config", "set", "systemctl", "user", "restart", "service"}
REACH_RANK = {"box": 0, "owner": 1, "member": 2, "public": 3, "outside-person": 4}
UNDO_RANK = {"minutes": 0, "hours": 1, "no": 2}
L, R = r"(?<![a-z0-9])", r"(?![a-z0-9])"   # word edges that also split on _ and -, so GH_TOKEN reads as a token


def W(words):
    return L + "(?:" + words + ")" + R


def parse_shape(text):
    """(kind, what, key) when the ask's whole text, stripped, is one shape; else None. Only printable ASCII and
    single spaces, so a second line, a tab or a look-alike letter never parses."""
    s = str(text or "").strip()
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[ -~]+", s) or "  " in s:
        return None
    for kind, rx in SHAPES:
        m = rx.fullmatch(s)
        if not m:
            continue
        if kind == "config":
            lo, hi = CONFIG_KEYS[m.group(1)]
            if not lo <= int(m.group(2)) <= hi:
                return None
            return kind, f"{m.group(1)}={int(m.group(2))}", m.group(1)
        return kind, m.group(1), None
    return None


UNSET = object()


def config_now(key):
    """KEY's value now, through cc-config with its environment pinned: the value, UNSET (get exits 1: no value), or
    None when it can't be read (any other exit, a timeout, no cc-config)."""
    if "config" in _TEST:
        return _TEST["config"].get(key, UNSET)
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([place("cc_config", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-config")),
                            "get", key], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20, env=config_env(),
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return p.stdout.rstrip("\n") if p.returncode == 0 else UNSET if p.returncode == 1 else None


def caller_undo(revert, key):
    """The caller's own revert as words when it is exactly an undo of KEY that the config shape itself would accept
    (`cc-config unset KEY`, or `cc-config set KEY N` with N a plain number in KEY's range), else None. A watcher runs
    the revert on its own, so an unchecked value never reaches it (planning's review of #1089: "Keep it only if
    parse_shape(shlex.join(words)) passes")."""
    try:
        words = shlex.split(squash(revert))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if words == ["cc-config", "unset", key]:
        return words
    shape = parse_shape(shlex.join(words)) if len(words) == 4 and words[1:3] == ["set", key] else None
    return words if shape and shape[2] == key else None


def unit_state(unit):
    """What `systemctl --user is-active cc-NAME.service` says now: "active", another state word, or "" when it can't
    be read. Read-only, and the binary is pinned, so a caller's PATH can't fake an active unit. Lander review of #1089:
    a restart of an inactive unit starts it, so "the unit runs as before" holds only for an active one."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([place("systemctl", "/usr/bin/systemctl"), "--user", "is-active", f"{unit}.service"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""
    s = p.stdout.strip()
    return s if re.fullmatch(r"[a-z-]{1,20}", s) and (s == "active") == (p.returncode == 0) else ""


def shape_undo(shape, revert):
    """(revert, note) for a grant: revert is a command a watcher may run, or "" when there is none to run; note says
    why when it is "". A restart has nothing to undo. A config key goes back to its value now (lane review of #1089:
    "If the key already had a value, restore that value instead"); the caller's own checked undo stands when it agrees,
    or when the value now can't be read. With neither, nothing runnable is recorded: tell, don't auto-revert."""
    if shape[0] != "config":
        return "", "nothing to undo: a restart of an active unit leaves it running as it was"
    key, old = shape[2], config_now(shape[2])
    theirs = caller_undo(revert, key)
    if old is None:
        if theirs:
            return shlex.join(theirs), ""
        return "", f"{key}'s value before couldn't be read, so no undo is recorded; check it by hand before undoing"
    mine = f"cc-config unset {key}" if old is UNSET else f"cc-config set {key} {shlex.quote(old)}"
    return mine, ""


# The hard lines, matched on the folded text (fold() below). Each is (name, pattern); a kind maps onto the same names.
HARD = [
    ("real money", r"[$€£¥]\s?\d|\d\s?[$€£¥]|" + W(r"usd|eur|euros?|dollars?|pounds?|gbp|cents?|payments?|pay|paid|paying|"
                   r"purchases?|buy|buying|order from|invoices?|subscriptions?|subscribe|credit card|debit|card on file|"
                   r"charge|charged|charges|billing|bill|refund|renewal|renew|spend|spending|budget|prices?|wallet|"
                   r"crypto|bitcoin|stripe|paypal|live (broker|trading|account)|real account|acquire|acquiring|amazon|orders?|"
                   r"ordering|checkout")),
    ("secrets and credentials", r"token|credential|passw|passwd|secret|api[ _-]?keys?|private[ _-]?keys?|ssh[ _-]?keys?|"
                                r"id_rsa|id_ed25519|id_ecdsa|\.env" + R + r"|\.netrc|hosts\.yml|\.config/gh|\.ssh|\.pem|"
                                r"\.p12|keyring|keychain|gpg|oauth|cookie|webhook url|signing key|bot\.json|\.cc/slack/|" + W("pat|pats")),
    # this box's own never-touch literals (its rescue IP) are not in core/: never_touch_rx() adds them from the overlay
    ("the never-touch list", r"rescue ip|rescue address|hotspot|arrival interface|resolv\.conf|/etc/hosts|" + W(
        r"firewall|ufw|iptables|nftables|nft|partitions?|fdisk|parted|mkfs|reboot|shutdown|poweroff|halt|"
        r"ip (link|addr|address|route|rule)|ifconfig|nmcli|iwconfig|wpa_supplicant|networkmanager|netplan|wlp\w*|"
        r"wlan\d|eth\d|enp\w+|dhcp|sysctl|modprobe|grub|bios|kernel|dpkg|apt|rfkill|wifi|wi-fi|bluetooth|nmcli\w*|"
        r"ip (l|a|r)")),
    ("unplanned deletion of shared state", W(r"rm|rmdir|unlink|shred|delete[sd]?|deleting|remove[sd]?|removing|erase|"
                                             r"wipe|purge|truncate|prune|drop|destroy|discard|overwrite|clobber|"
                                             r"git clean|reset --hard|filter-branch|filter-repo|--delete|--mirror|"
                                             r"--force|-f|mv|update-ref") + r"|force[ -]?push|branch\s+-d|"
                                             r"push\s+\S+\s+\+|push\s+\S+\s+\+?:|(?:^|\s):?\s*>(?!>)\s*[~/$]"),
    ("widening a non-owner", W(r"members?|non-owner|workspaces?|guests?|collaborators?|teammates?|contractors?|"
                               r"clients?|customers?|invite[sd]?|invitation|maintainers?|chmod|chown|setfacl|usermod|useradd|adduser|"
                               r"groupadd|gpasswd|sudoers|visudo|"
                               r"write access|push access|admin access") + r"|" + W(r"give|grant|add|allow|let") +
                             r".{0,40}" + W(r"write|admin|push|access|roles?|permissions?|read|maintain|triage")),
    ("mail or posts in his name", r"[a-z0-9._%+-]+@[a-z0-9.-]+\.[a-z]{2,}|in (his|her|their|the owner'?s) name|"
                                  r"as (him|her|them|the owner|the user)" + R + r"|on (his|her|their|the owner'?s) behalf|" +
                                  W(r"e-?mails?|e-?mailing|mail|mails|mailing|dm|dms|tweet|replies|reply|respond|"
                                    r"comments?|announce|newsletter|sms|whatsapp|linkedin|twitter|"
                                    r"upstream|outreach|curl|wget|gh issue|gh pr|gh api") + r"|" + W(r"send|sends|sending|post|posts|posting") +
                                  r".{0,60}" + W(r"to|on|in")),
    ("opening the host", W(r"ssh|sshd|authorized_keys|sftp|scp|rsync|telnet|vnc|rdp|socat|netcat|nc|ncat|ngrok|"
                           r"tailscale|zerotier|wireguard|wg|vpn|frp|tunnels?|cloudflared|port[ -]?forward\w*|"
                           r"reverse shell|bind shell|shell access|connectors?|expose[sd]?|exposing|listen|listening|"
                           r"lan|wan|host port|open (a |the )?port|upnp|dmz|bind|bound|every interface|all interfaces|"
                           r"http\.server|--host|--publish|-p \d+:\d+") + r"|0\.0\.0\.0"),
    ("code from outside the box", r"\|\s*(?:sudo\s+)?(?:sh|bash|zsh|dash|python3?|perl|ruby|node)" + R + r"|" +
                                  W(r"base64 -d|base64 --decode|eval")),
    # Perms' standing condition, now in code: "any ask that touches perms' own CLAUDE.md or settings, ~/.cc/approvals,
    # hooks, the guard, the sandbox or bwrap, or autoMode is always the owner's." cc-config is one unless it is the
    # config shape's own command on a listed key.
    ("the box's own controls", r"claude\.md|\.claude/|approvals|allow[ -]?list|allow rules?|guard|bwrap|bubblewrap|"
                               r"sandbox|automode|auto[ -]mode|crosssessioninbound|dangerously|seccomp|apparmor|"
                               r"sudo|setuid|polkit|cc-approve|cc-infer|ld_preload|ld_library_path|bashrc|zshrc|\.profile|~/bin|"
                               r"/usr/local/bin|send-keys|" +
                               L + r"cc-config(?! set (?:" + "|".join(CONFIG_KEYS).lower() + r") \d{1,6}$)|" +
                               W(r"settings?|settings[\w.-]*|hooks?|fence|perms|permissions?|bypass|/allow|cc_tier|tier|"
                                 r"spend|cc-msg|tmux|shim|shims|path|claude")),
    # Architect, 10-11 (third security read): "docker or any container run, crontab-style or every-N schedules,
    # stopping or disabling a box daemon, pushes to main or any default branch, writes to ~/.cc/config or ~/.cc/env,
    # and copying either of those anywhere."
    ("a container run", W(r"docker|podman|containerd|nerdctl|ctr|kubectl|k8s|kubernetes|helm|lxc|lxd|incus|runc|crun|"
                          r"buildah|containers?|compose|nspawn|systemd-nspawn|singularity|apptainer|firecracker|qemu|kvm|"
                          r"virsh|vagrant")),
    ("a recurring schedule", W(r"cron|crontab|cronjob|anacron|timers?|oncalendar|every|hourly|daily|weekly|monthly|"
                               r"nightly|weekdays?|periodic\w*|recurring|repeat\w*|intervals?|systemd-run|at now|at \d+|batch|watch|"
                               r"loop|forever|sleep") + r"|\*/\d|@(?:reboot|hourly|daily|weekly|monthly|yearly|annually|midnight)"),
    ("stopping or disabling a daemon", W(r"stop|stops|stopping|stopped|disable[sd]?|disabling|mask|masked|masking|kill|"
                                         r"kills|killall|pkill|killing|pause|suspend|freeze|sigterm|sigkill|sigstop|"
                                         r"terminate|terminating|shut down|turn off|switch off")),
    ("a push to main or a default branch", W(r"push|pushes|pushing|pushed|merge|merges|merging|merged|main|master|trunk|"
                                             r"default branch")),
    ("~/.cc/config or ~/.cc/env", r"\.cc[\s/\\.]*(?:config|env)" + R + r"|" + W(r"cc_config|cc_config_deny|cc_env")),
]
HARD_RE = [(n, re.compile(p)) for n, p in HARD]
SECRET_RE = dict(HARD_RE)["secrets and credentials"]
# What the hard lines and the ports don't read (perms, 10-12: "no secrets", "no member widening", "03:21Z" and
# "origin/main" each sent a one-off promote to the owner): a negated clause of plain words that ends where the clause
# does, a Z-stamped or dated time, and a ref ending in a default branch. Only these are masked, so a verb beside them
# still matches ("merge origin/main", "push ..., no review"), a clause that runs on into more words isn't masked ("no
# problem rm -rf ~"), and a bare "at 03:21" is still an at job.
_WORD = r"[a-z]+(?:'[a-z]+)?"
_PHRASE = _WORD + r"(?:[\s-]+" + _WORD + r"){0,2}"
UNREAD = re.compile(
    L + r"(?:no|without|never|nor|zero)\s+" + _PHRASE + r"(?:\s+(?:or|nor)\s+" + _PHRASE + r")*" +
    r"(?=\s*(?:[,;.!?)]|$)|\s+(?:and|but|then|so|yet|while|because)" + R + r")"
    r"|" + L + r"(?:\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}[t ])?\d{1,2}:\d{2}(?::\d{2})?(?:\.\d+)?z" + R +
    r"|" + L + r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}[t ]\d{1,2}:\d{2}(?::\d{2})?" + R +
    r"|" + L + r"[\w.-]+/(?:main|master|trunk)" + R)


def unread(t):
    """The folded text with what UNREAD names blanked out: what the hard lines and the ports are matched on."""
    return squash(UNREAD.sub(" ", t))
_NEVER = {}

# Owner, 10-12, of a card asking him to copy a client id the box already held into a site's Pages env: "why are my
# approvals needed for these things?? I approve them blindly anyways". So moving or copying a credential the box
# ALREADY holds between its own services (env files, cc-config, a unit's environment, a Pages or Workers env) is
# perms' call, not his. Minting or rotating one stays his, and perms refuses a copy that
# widens who can read it (a member workspace, anything public, a log). credential_move() reads which one an ask is.
CRED_WIDEN = re.compile(W(r"members?|workspaces?|guests?|third[ -]part(?:y|ies)|collaborators?|contractors?|"
                          r"customers?|outsiders?|public\w*|publish\w*|gists?|pastebin|logs?|logged|logging|stdout|"
                          r"stderr|readme|commit\w*|slack|channels?|threads?|issues?|comments?|screenshots?|"
                          r"share[sd]?|sharing|e-?mail\w*|mail\w*"))
CRED_MINT = re.compile(W(r"mint\w*|rotat\w*|regenerat\w*|generat\w*|creat\w*|revok\w*|reissu\w*|roll|rolls|rolled|"
                         r"rolling|reset\w*|renew\w*|re-?keys?|re-?keying|new|fresh|register\w*|sign(?:ing)? up"))
CRED_MOVE = re.compile(W(r"cop(?:y|ies|ied|ying)|mov(?:e|es|ed|ing)|sync\w*|set|sets|setting|put|puts|putting|"
                         r"store[sd]?|storing|add|adds|added|adding|wire[sd]?|wiring"))
CRED_DEST = re.compile(r"cc-config|" + W(r"env|envs|environment|dotenv|systemd|units?|services?|pages|workers?|"
                                         r"wrangler|cloudflare"))
CRED_INTO = re.compile(W(r"into|to|onto|in"))
# the destination stretch ends where the ask turns to the value or its source; every piece of it, split on and/then/
# so/commas, must name one of the box's services (security read of #1214: only the first one was read)
CRED_UNTIL = re.compile(W(r"from|with|for"))
CRED_PIECE = re.compile(W(r"and|then|so|plus|also|or") + r"|[,;&+]")
CRED_PUT = re.compile(r"wrangler (?:pages )?secret put" + R)
# a path is never one of the box's own services (security read of #1214: /tmp/env, a member's ~/dev/<name>/.env)
CRED_PATH = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.-])(?:~|\.{1,2})?/\S|\S/\S*/|(?<![a-z0-9])\.env" + R)
# env names a site build ships to its client code, so anyone who loads the page reads the value
CRED_CLIENT = re.compile(L + r"(?:vite|react_app|next_public|expo_public|nuxt_public|gatsby|public)_[a-z0-9_]+")


def credential_dest_ok(t):
    """Every place the ask copies into is one of the box's own services: each stretch after into/to/onto/in, up to a
    from/with/for, is split on and/then/so/commas, and every piece names one; there is at least one (or the command
    is `wrangler secret put` itself), and no path appears anywhere in the ask."""
    if CRED_PATH.search(t):
        return False
    pieces = [p for m in CRED_INTO.finditer(t) for p in CRED_PIECE.split(CRED_UNTIL.split(t[m.end():], 1)[0])]
    return all(CRED_DEST.search(p) for p in pieces) and bool(pieces or CRED_PUT.search(t))


def member_names():
    """The member workspaces' names (~/.cc/members/<name> without the owner-workspace marker), each with its first
    part, so "so robin can use it" reads as the member robin-example (security read of #1214)."""
    members = place("members", f"{HOME}/.cc/members")
    try:
        names = [n for n in os.listdir(members) if re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", n)
                 and os.path.isdir(f"{members}/{n}") and not os.path.isfile(f"{members}/{n}/owner-workspace")]
    except OSError:
        names = []
    out = set()
    for n in names:
        out.add(n.casefold())
        first = re.split(r"[._-]", n.casefold())[0]
        if len(first) >= 3:
            out.add(first)
    return out


# the only other hard line an own-service move may cross: the box's controls on the word cc-config, which is where
# the box holds such a value. A path to ~/.cc/config or ~/.cc/env names the whole file, so that line still holds.
CRED_MOVE_ALSO = {"the box's own controls": "cc-config"}


ENV_NAME = re.compile(r"(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*(?:_[A-Z0-9]+)+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])")


def credential_move(a, t):
    """For an ask whose own text names a credential: "widen" for a copy that widens who can read it (by its words, a
    member's name, an env name a site ships to its client code, or a `reaches` claim past the owner; perms refuses
    it), "box" for a move of a held one between the box's own services (perms' call), else None (still the owner's: a
    mint or rotation, a path, another hard line, or anything this can't read as a move)."""
    # a credential named in a negated clause is none ("no secrets", #1202); the rest reads the whole text, stricter
    if not SECRET_RE.search(unread(t)):
        return None
    if (CRED_WIDEN.search(t) or CRED_CLIENT.search(t) or REACH_RANK.get(a.get("reaches"), 0) > REACH_RANK["owner"]
            or any(re.search(W(re.escape(n)), t) for n in member_names())):
        return "widen"
    # The mint words and the hard lines are read on the whole text, env names included (GENERATED_API_TOKEN is a
    # mint, PUSH_TO_ORIGIN_MAIN a push). The mask is only for a non-owner word inside an env name, since CLIENT in
    # LIBRARY_FEEDBACK_CLIENT_ID is no client, and for reading the move and its places (TO in an env name is no "to").
    if CRED_MINT.search(t):
        return None
    masked = fold(ENV_NAME.sub("the value", str(a.get("ask") or "")))
    if not (CRED_MOVE.search(masked) and credential_dest_ok(masked)):
        return None
    hard = [h for h in hard_lines(a, t) if h[0] != "widening a non-owner"]
    hard += [h for h in hard_lines(a, masked) if h[0] == "widening a non-owner"]
    for n, _ in hard:
        if n == "secrets and credentials":
            continue
        # every match of the line, not the first one hard_lines() keeps: "from cc-config into the hooks env" is a
        # hook as well as cc-config (security read of #1214)
        rx = dict(HARD_RE).get(n)
        if CRED_MOVE_ALSO.get(n) is None or rx is None or \
                any(m.group(0).strip() != CRED_MOVE_ALSO[n] for m in rx.finditer(t)):
            return None
    return "box"


def never_touch_path():
    """The box's own never-touch literals, one per line, in the private overlay beside core/ (config/never-touch.txt),
    found the way cc-name finds config/names.json. No environment override: a caller can't point it elsewhere."""
    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    default = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(root), "config", "never-touch.txt") if os.path.basename(root) == "core" else ""
    return place("never_touch", default)


def never_touch_rx():
    """A pattern for the overlay's literals, None when there is no file (the generic words still apply), or False when
    the file is there but can't be read, which fails closed."""
    p = never_touch_path()
    if p not in _NEVER:
        try:
            with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                lits = [fold(ln) for ln in f if fold(ln) and not ln.lstrip().startswith("#")]
            _NEVER[p] = re.compile("|".join(re.escape(x) for x in lits)) if lits else None
        except FileNotFoundError:
            _NEVER[p] = None
        except (OSError, UnicodeError):
            _NEVER[p] = False
    return _NEVER[p]
KIND_HARD = {"money": "real money", "secret": "secrets and credentials", "never-touch": "the never-touch list",
             "delete-shared": "unplanned deletion of shared state", "widen-member": "widening a non-owner",
             "open-host": "opening the host", "controls": "the box's own controls", "mail": "mail or posts in his name",
             "post": "mail or posts in his name"}
PORTS = re.compile(r"(?:" + W("port|ports") + r"\s*:?\s*|:)(\d{1,5})" + R)
ZERO_WIDTH = re.compile("[­͏؜ᅟᅠ឴឵᠎​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤⁪-⁯﻿]")
# lowercase letters from other scripts that read as Latin ones (the Cyrillic e in "sеttings")
CONFUSABLE = str.maketrans("аеёорсухіїјѕһԁӏԛԝкмнтвьαοερικνυτχβηϲϳ", "aeeopcyxiijshdlqwkmhtbbaoepikvutxbncj")
GRANT_ITEM = re.compile(r"^grant:([1-9])$")
TICKET = re.compile(r"^T\d{8}T\d{6}-[0-9a-f]{1,8}$")
MIN_QUOTE = 20
# words that carry no intent, so a quote that shares only these with the ask is no evidence for it
STOPWORDS = set("""about above after again against also because been before being below between both could does doing
down during each from further have having here into itself just more most must need only other over please same should
some such than that their them then there these they this those through under until very want were what when where which
while will with would your yours make sure keep thing things want wants like going""".split())


def squash(s):
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", str(s or "")).strip()


def fold(s):
    """NFKC, drop zero-width and bidi marks, map look-alike letters to Latin, strip accents, casefold: what the hard
    lines are matched on, so a full-width, accented or Cyrillic spelling reads as the word it imitates."""
    s = ZERO_WIDTH.sub("", unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", str(s or ""))).casefold().translate(CONFUSABLE)
    s = "".join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))
    return squash(s)


def foreign_letters(s):
    """Letters that are still not Latin after fold(): text the rules can't read, so nothing is granted on it."""
    return any(ord(c) > 127 and unicodedata.category(c).startswith("L") for c in s)


def text_ports(t):
    return {int(p) for p in PORTS.findall(t)}


def hard_lines(a, t):
    """Every hard line the ask crosses, by its folded text or its kind, each with the word that matched it, so whoever
    reads the reason sees why (lane review of #1089: the lists stay wide because the decider fails closed, but the
    reason names the word). The stricter reading wins."""
    kind, hits = a.get("kind") or "", {}
    for n, rx in HARD_RE:
        m = rx.search(t)
        if m and n not in hits:
            hits[n] = m.group(0).strip()
    nt = never_touch_rx()
    if "the never-touch list" not in hits:
        m = nt.search(t) if nt else None
        if m or nt is False:
            hits["the never-touch list"] = m.group(0) if m else "the box's never-touch file, which can't be read"
    m = PORTS.search(t)
    if m and "opening the host" not in hits:
        hits["opening the host"] = m.group(0).strip()
    for n, on, word in ((KIND_HARD.get(kind), kind in KIND_HARD, f"kind {kind}"),
                        ("real money", a.get("money") is True, "money true"),
                        ("secrets and credentials", a.get("data") == "secret", "data secret")):
        if on and n not in hits:
            hits[n] = word
    return list(hits.items())


def config_env():
    """cc-config's environment, pinned: the account's home and its own ~/.cc/config, nothing denied, so the caller
    can't choose the owner-repo list (security read, 10-11)."""
    return {"HOME": HOME, "CC_CONFIG": f"{HOME}/.cc/config", "CC_CONFIG_DENY": "", "PATH": "/usr/bin:/bin",
            "LC_ALL": "C.UTF-8"}


def owner_repos():
    """The owner's own repos: the names in CC_JANITOR_REPOS in his ~/.cc/config (read through cc-config with its
    environment pinned), less any name that is a member workspace (~/.cc/members/<name> without the host-side
    owner-workspace marker). A member's ~/.cc/state/<handle>/goals.md is writable from inside its sandbox, so it never
    counts as his (security read, 10-11), and a name not on the list counts as nothing."""
    if "repos" in _TEST:
        names = _TEST["repos"]
    else:
        try:
            p = subprocess.run([os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-config"), "get",
                                "CC_JANITOR_REPOS"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20, env=config_env(),
                               stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
            names = p.stdout.split() if p.returncode == 0 else []
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            names = []
    members = place("members", f"{HOME}/.cc/members")
    return {n for n in names if re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", n)
            and (not os.path.isdir(f"{members}/{n}") or os.path.isfile(f"{members}/{n}/owner-workspace"))}


def goals_file_ok(path, repos):
    """Goals come only from ~/.cc/state/<repo>/goals.md for one of the owner's own repos, never from a member
    workspace's state dir, anywhere under ~/dev/ or a scratch dir."""
    real = os.path.realpath(path)
    root = os.path.realpath(place("state", f"{HOME}/.cc/state"))
    dev = os.path.realpath(f"{HOME}/dev")
    return (os.path.basename(real) == "goals.md" and os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(real)) == root
            and not (real + "/").startswith(dev + "/") and os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(real)) in repos)


def evidence_lines(text, floor=MIN_QUOTE):
    """The lines a quote may come from: no heading, no line under `floor` characters once its bullet is gone."""
    out = []
    for ln in str(text or "").split("\n"):
        s = re.sub(r"^\s*(?:[-*+>]|\d+[.)])\s+", "", ln).strip()
        if s and not s.startswith("#") and len(s) >= floor:
            out.append(fold(s))
    return out


def content_words(s, drop):
    return {w for w in re.findall(r"[a-z][a-z0-9]*", fold(s)) if len(w) >= 4 and w not in STOPWORDS and w not in drop}


def related(quote, ask, repos):
    """The quote and the ask share a content word: not a stopword, a shape's own word or a repo name. A word counts
    when one is the other or begins it (slack, slackd)."""
    drop = SHAPE_WORDS | {r.lower() for r in repos}
    qw, aw = content_words(quote, drop), content_words(ask, drop)
    return any(x == y or x.startswith(y) or y.startswith(x) for x in qw for y in aw)


def names_the_shape(quote, ask):
    """Does the quote name the ask's own key or unit, every word of it whole (cc and service aside)? A Slack message
    is his ordinary chat, so a shared word or a 4-letter prefix is not enough there: "I think we should wait" shares
    "think" with CC_ASK_THINK, "Turn it off" begins "turns", "Slack is noisy" begins "slackd" (Opus security read of
    #1129: "For a Slack source, require the exact key or unit word"). A unit is named by its whole name, so cc-slackd-old
    is not cc-slackd. An ask that is no shape names nothing, so fails."""
    shape = parse_shape(squash(ask))
    if shape and shape[0] == "service":
        # a path is no unit: ~/cc-slackd/x names a folder (Opus read of #1129 at cc8323ea)
        return bool(re.search(rf"(?<![a-z0-9_.~/-]){re.escape(shape[1].lower())}(?:\.service)?(?![a-z0-9_/-]|\.[a-z0-9])",
                              fold(quote)))
    words = {w for w in re.split(r"[^a-z0-9]+", (shape[2] or shape[1]).lower()) if w not in ("", "cc", "service")} \
        if shape else set()
    return bool(words) and words <= set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", fold(quote)))


def grant_item(n):
    """Item n of the owner's one-time grant (2026-09-21), from the host rules next to this tool."""
    p = place("grants", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "..", "..", "docs", "host-rules.md"))
    try:
        lines = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
    except OSError:
        return ""
    on = False
    for ln in lines:
        if "one-time grant**" in ln:
            on = True; continue
        m = re.match(r"^\s+(\d+)\.\s+(.*)", ln)
        if on and m and int(m.group(1)) == n:
            return m.group(2)
        if on and ln.startswith("- "):
            break
    return ""


SLACK_SRC = re.compile(r"^slack:([CDG][A-Z0-9]{2,})/(\d{6,}\.\d{1,6})$")
GOAL_SRC = re.compile(r"[\s(\[]*\bsrc:\s*(\S+?)[)\]]*\s*$")


def slack_call(method, **params):
    """One Slack Web API read with the bot token; raises on a refusal. selfcheck() swaps in a fake, so it never calls out."""
    if "slack_api" in _TEST:
        return _TEST["slack_api"](method, **params)
    import urllib.parse, urllib.request
    tok = config_now("SLACK_BOT_TOKEN")
    if not isinstance(tok, str) or not tok:
        raise RuntimeError("no SLACK_BOT_TOKEN")
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"https://slack.com/api/{method}", data=urllib.parse.urlencode(params).encode(),
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {tok}"})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as r:
        out = json.loads(r.read().decode())
    if not out.get("ok"):
        raise RuntimeError(f"{method}: {out.get('error')}")
    return out


def slack_owner():
    owner = _TEST["slack_owner"] if "slack_owner" in _TEST else config_now("SLACK_OWNER_ID")
    return owner if isinstance(owner, str) and re.fullmatch(r"[UW][A-Z0-9]{2,}", owner) else ""


def ledger_deleted(chat, ts):
    """Has the daemon recorded his deletion of this message? The ledger is a cache any session could write, so it is
    read for one thing only: a deletion, which can only take a goal away, never give one."""
    try:
        with open(place("owner_words", f"{HOME}/.cc/state/owner-words.jsonl"), encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            for ln in f:
                try:
                    r = json.loads(ln)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("event") == "delete" and r.get("channel") == chat and r.get("ts") == ts:
                    return True
    except OSError:
        pass
    return False


def fetch_slack(chat, ts):
    """The message at chat/ts as Slack holds it now, or None. conversations.history finds a top-level message (as
    cc-slack's fetch_message does). A thread reply isn't in it, so this is cc-slack's reacted_message read, which
    already reads channel thread replies with the bot token: conversations.replies for the reply's ts names its thread
    (thread_ts), and a second read anchored at that parent with oldest=ts, inclusive, comes back parent first and then
    the reply (the parent doesn't count against limit), which the ts filter picks out."""
    try:
        m = (slack_call("conversations.history", channel=chat, latest=ts, inclusive="true", limit="1").get("messages")
             or [None])[0]
        if m and m.get("ts") == ts:
            return m
        head = slack_call("conversations.replies", channel=chat, ts=ts, limit="1").get("messages") or []
        if not head:
            return None
        root = head[0].get("thread_ts") or head[0].get("ts")
        if root == ts:
            return next((x for x in head if x.get("ts") == ts), None)
        msgs = slack_call("conversations.replies", channel=chat, ts=root, oldest=ts, inclusive="true",
                          limit="1").get("messages") or []
        return next((x for x in msgs if x.get("ts") == ts and (x.get("thread_ts") or x.get("ts")) == root), None)
    except Exception:
        return None


CUT = "\x00"     # where text that isn't his statement was taken out of a sentence: a boundary no quote crosses


def unmark(text):
    """Slack's markup read as the words he sees, so a quote of what Slack shows matches the text Slack stores:
    <url|text> is its text, <url> the url, <#C…|name> #name, *bold* and _italic_ their words. What isn't his statement
    leaves a CUT, never a space, so taking it out joins no words (dropping "`no`" from "Give cc-ask `no` more turns"
    must not leave "Give cc-ask more turns", #1129 review): code, ~struck~ text (words he struck out) and a mention
    (<@U…>, <!here>). &gt; &lt; &amp; are unescaped last, so a < he typed stays text."""
    t = str(text or "")
    t = re.sub(r"```.*?```", CUT, t, flags=re.S)
    t = re.sub(r"`[^`\n]*`", CUT, t)
    t = re.sub(r"<#[CG][A-Z0-9]+\|([^<>\n]*)>", r"#\1", t)
    t = re.sub(r"<[@!#][^<>\n]*>", CUT, t)
    t = re.sub(r"<[^<>|\n]+\|([^<>\n]+)>", r"\1", t)
    t = re.sub(r"<([^<>|\n]+)>", r"\1", t)
    for mark, keep in (("*", r"\1"), ("_", r"\1"), ("~", CUT)):
        m = re.escape(mark)
        t = re.sub(rf"(?<![\w{m}]){m}([^\s{m}](?:[^{m}\n]*[^\s{m}])?){m}(?![\w{m}])", keep, t)
    return t.replace("&gt;", ">").replace("&lt;", "<").replace("&amp;", "&")


def sentence(s):
    """Text folded for matching."""
    return fold(squash(s))


# what Slack lets a person post on his behalf: his own message, one also sent to the channel, one with a file
HIS_SUBTYPES = (None, "", "thread_broadcast", "file_share")
# a stop inside his one sentence, code he left open, or a question mark: then it is no single plain go
STOPS = re.compile("[.!;:\u2026`?\u203d\u061f\u00bf\u2e2e\u2047-\u2049\uff1f\ufe56]")
# a word that can turn his line into a refusal or a condition, anywhere in the message: then nothing in it grants
# (security read of #1129: "fail closed and keep it simple"). n't with any apostrophe, and the same words typed bare.
# Then the words that hand his line to someone else or take it back (round 4: "Bob asked me this today", "If Bob
# agrees", "Just kidding"), a time or a condition (round 4: "… once the review lands"), and a sentence that
# opens like a question though it carries no ? ("Should we …").
HEDGE = re.compile(r"\b(?:not|never|no|nope|nah|unless|until|only|but|wait|hold|cannot|dont|doesnt|didnt|isnt|arent|"
                   r"wasnt|werent|wont|cant|shouldnt|wouldnt|couldnt|havent|hasnt|hadnt|aint|mustnt|neednt|"
                   r"if|whether|maybe|perhaps|might|suppose|supposing|assuming|provided|unsure|"
                   r"kidding|joking|joke|jk|scratch|ignore|disregard|cancel|retract|undo|forget|"
                   r"asked|asks|asking|said|says|wrote|writes|wants|wanted|requested|suggested|suggests|proposed|"
                   r"wonder|wondering|thoughts|reject|rejected|rejecting|refuse|refused|deny|denied|decline|declined|veto|vetoed|"
                   r"once|when|whenever|after|before|later|tomorrow|tonight|soon|eventually|yet|"
                   # Opus delta read of #1129 at f9fcd778: a go verb with a particle is its opposite ("Give up on …",
                   # "Set aside …"), and a refusal or a laugh in another tongue stops a grant as "not" does
                   r"up|aside|away|off|apart|"
                   r"nicht|nein|kein|keine|nee|non|pas|nunca|nada|nyet|niet|lol|lmao|lmfao|rofl|haha\w*|hehe\w*|nvm)\b"
                   r"|n['`\u2018\u2019\u02bc\u00b4]t\b"
                   r"|(?:^|[.!:;,\n]\s*)(?:should|could|would|can|will|shall|do|does|did|is|are|was|were|may|must|"
                   r"what|why|how|which|who|whom|whose|where|any)\b")


def hedged(text):
    """Does a negation or condition word stand anywhere in his message, raw or folded (so markup, code, a link's text
    or a look-alike letter hides none)? _ is a word character to \\b, so it is read as a space: _Hold_ is "hold"."""
    t = str(text or "").replace("_", " ")
    return any(HEDGE.search(x) for x in (t.casefold(), fold(t)))


def his_go(text):
    """His whole message as the one sentence it must be, folded and without its final . or !, or '' when it is
    anything else (round 4 of #1129: "a Slack quote grants ONLY when his WHOLE message is that one sentence"). One line,
    one sentence (no stop, colon or question mark inside it, no code, no mention, no struck text). So a `>` quote, a
    list item, a second line ("… \nAfter the review lands.") or a speaker ("Bob: give …") is no go; go_template()
    then reads what the sentence says."""
    t = sentence(unmark(unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", str(text or ""))).strip())
    body = t.rstrip(" .!")
    if len(unmark(str(text or "")).strip().splitlines()) > 1 or CUT in body or STOPS.search(body):
        return ""
    # only plain words, digits and their joiners: an emoji (🚫, 👎) or a sign beside the value (~16, <16, 16+) may
    # carry his meaning, so it is no plain go (Opus delta read of #1129 at f9fcd778)
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9 ,'_-]+", body):
        return ""
    return body


def said(text, quote):
    """Is the quote his whole message, the one plain go his_go() reads (only a final . or ! may be left off)?"""
    go = his_go(text)
    return bool(go) and sentence(unmark(quote)).rstrip(" .!") == go


def go_templates(ask):
    """The few whole sentences that are his go for this ask (#1129 follow-up: an opening verb let "Give up on cc-ask 16
    turns", "Approve cc-slackd's PR" and "Give cc-ask 16 turns and we blow the budget" through). For a key, its words
    after cc (CC_ASK_TURNS: ask, turns), cc optional and joined by -, _ or a space: "set <key words> to N" and "give
    <key words but the last> N <last word>", N the ask's value exactly. For a unit, "restart <unit>". Nothing may follow,
    so a time, a reason or a second clause ("next week", "and we blow the budget") is never a go."""
    shape = parse_shape(squash(ask))
    if not shape:
        return []
    if shape[0] == "service":
        return [rf"restart {re.escape(shape[1].lower())}(?:\.service)?"]
    words, n = shape[2].lower().split("_")[1:], re.escape(shape[1].split("=", 1)[1])
    name = lambda ws: r"(?:cc[-_ ])?" + "[-_ ]".join(map(re.escape, ws))
    return [rf"set {name(words)} to {n}", rf"give {name(words[:-1])} {n} {re.escape(words[-1])}"]


def go_template(text, ask):
    """Is his whole message, as his_go() reads it, exactly one of the ask's go templates? Anything else is perms'."""
    go = his_go(text)
    return bool(go) and any(re.fullmatch(t, go) for t in go_templates(ask))


def check_slack(chat, ts, quote, ask):
    """('', his message's whole text) when the message at chat/ts, fetched from Slack now, is the owner's own, it
    names the ask's own key or unit, no negation or condition word stands anywhere in it, and the quote is his whole
    message, one sentence that is exactly a go template for the ask (go_templates()). Otherwise (the reason it isn't, '').
    The owner-words ledger is only a cache, so a line forged into it grants nothing; a deletion it records still
    revokes the goal."""
    if ledger_deleted(chat, ts):
        return "he deleted that Slack message, so the goal citing it no longer stands", ""
    owner = slack_owner()
    if not owner:
        return "the owner's Slack id can't be read, so no Slack citation can be checked", ""
    m = fetch_slack(chat, ts)
    if not m or m.get("subtype") == "tombstone":
        return "that Slack message can't be fetched now (deleted, or not readable by the bot)", ""
    if m.get("bot_id") or m.get("user") != owner:
        return "that Slack message is not the owner's own", ""
    if m.get("subtype") not in HIS_SUBTYPES:
        return f"that Slack message is a {str(m.get('subtype'))[:40]} event, not something he wrote", ""
    if any(unicodedata.category(c) in ("Cc", "Cf") for c in quote):
        return "the quote carries invisible or control characters, so it isn't what he sees", ""
    if not names_the_shape(quote, ask):
        return "the quote doesn't name the ask's own key or unit, and a word in his chat is not enough", ""
    if hedged(m.get("text")):
        return ("his message carries a negation, condition, retraction or someone else's words (not, n't, if, "
                "kidding, asked, …) or opens a sentence like a question, so no line of it is read as a go"), ""
    if not said(m.get("text"), quote):
        return "the quote is not his whole statement: his whole message must be the quote, one sentence", ""
    if not go_template(m.get("text"), ask):
        return ("his message is not one of the go templates for this ask, with its value and nothing after it: "
                "'set <key words> to N', 'give <key words> N <noun>' or 'restart <unit>'"), ""
    return "", str(m.get("text") or "")


def check_evidence(evs, ask, cited_ok=False):
    """The evidence that holds: a quote of MIN_QUOTE characters or more (or a whole go template, which the Slack check
    holds to his whole message) that shares a content word with the ask and is in one counted line of the owner's
    state-dir goals.md, a Slack message of his, or item N of his one-time grant. `cited_ok` (the
    backtest) takes any sourced quote in place of the file lookup, since the files of the day are gone; the length and
    the shared word still hold."""
    good, bad, repos = [], [], None
    for e in evs if isinstance(evs, list) else []:
        e = e if isinstance(e, dict) else {}
        q, src = squash(e.get("quote")), str(e.get("source") or "").strip()

        def verdict(ok, why, message=""):
            # design: "The grant record keeps the full message, so whoever reads the ledger later can see what the
            # quote came from"
            (good if ok else bad).append(dict({"quote": q, "source": src}, **({"message": message} if message else {}))
                                         if ok else {"source": src, "why": why})
        if not q or not src:
            verdict(False, "no quote or no source"); continue
        # the Slack check matches sentence(unmark(q)), so the length and the shared word hold for that string too:
        # "<https://example.org/turns|OK.>" passes on its url's word and matches as "OK." (#1129 review)
        seen = (q, sentence(unmark(q)))
        # a quote that is a whole go template is checked as his whole message, so its length proves nothing either
        # way: "Restart cc-slackd." is a go under MIN_QUOTE, in his message or its goals.md line. A grant item and
        # the backtest never read it that way.
        whole = not cited_ok and not GRANT_ITEM.match(src) and any(re.fullmatch(t, seen[1].rstrip(" .!"))
                                                                    for t in go_templates(ask))
        if any(len(s) < MIN_QUOTE for s in seen) and not whole:
            verdict(False, f"a quote under {MIN_QUOTE} characters proves nothing"); continue
        if repos is None:
            repos = owner_repos() if not cited_ok else set()
        if not all(related(s, ask, repos) for s in seen):
            verdict(False, "the quote shares no content word with the ask"); continue
        if cited_ok:
            verdict(True, ""); continue
        g = GRANT_ITEM.match(src)
        if g:
            verdict(any(fold(q) in ln for ln in evidence_lines(grant_item(int(g.group(1))))),
                    "the quote is not in that item of the one-time grant")
        elif TICKET.match(src):
            # Architect, 10-11: "tickets.log carries no message, so a ticket only counts if the quote comes from the
            # message the ticket answers. If you can't resolve that, the ticket doesn't count as evidence."
            verdict(False, "a ticket can't be tied to the message it answered (tickets.log records none)")
        elif SLACK_SRC.match(src):
            why, text = check_slack(*SLACK_SRC.match(src).groups(), q, ask)
            verdict(not why, why, text)
        elif os.path.basename(src) == "goals.md":
            path = os.path.expanduser(src.replace("~", HOME, 1) if src.startswith("~") else src)
            if not goals_file_ok(path, repos):
                verdict(False, "goals count only from ~/.cc/state/<repo>/goals.md of the owner's own repos"); continue
            try:
                raw = open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read().split("\n")
            except OSError:
                raw = []
            # design, 10-12: goals.md is an index, not an authority. A line grants only through its own
            # `src: slack:<channel>/<ts>`, checked live; one with no src still steers the seat but grants nothing.
            hits = [ln for ln in raw if any(fold(q) in e for e in evidence_lines(GOAL_SRC.sub("", ln),
                                                                                 0 if whole else MIN_QUOTE))]
            srcs = [GOAL_SRC.search(ln).group(1) for ln in hits if GOAL_SRC.search(ln)]
            whys = [check_slack(*SLACK_SRC.match(s).groups(), q, ask) if SLACK_SRC.match(s) else
                    (f"its src: {s} is not slack:<channel>/<ts>", "") for s in srcs]
            if not hits:
                verdict(False, "the quote is not in one counted line of that goals.md")
            elif not srcs:
                verdict(False, "that goals.md line carries no src:, so it steers the seat's own work but grants nothing")
            else:
                verdict(any(not w for w, _ in whys), "; ".join(w for w, _ in whys if w),
                        next((t for w, t in whys if not w), ""))
        else:
            verdict(False, "not a goals.md, slack:<channel>/<ts> or grant:N")
    return good, bad


def decide(a, cited_ok=False):
    a = dict(a or {})
    t = fold(a.get("ask"))
    out = {"verdict": "", "reasons": [], "evidence": [], "evidence_refused": [], "ask": squash(a.get("ask"))}

    def done(v, *why, who="perms"):
        out["verdict"] = v; out["reasons"] += list(why)
        if v == "ASK-OWNER":
            out["who"] = who
        return out
    if not out["ask"]:
        return done("REFUSE", "no ask text")
    if a.get("owner_refused"):
        return done("REFUSE", f"the owner already refused this: {a['owner_refused']}")
    if 22 in text_ports(unread(t)) or str(a.get("port") or "").strip() == "22":
        return done("REFUSE", "port 22 is SSH into the host, never a site's app port")
    if foreign_letters(t):
        return done("ASK-OWNER", "the ask has letters the rules can't read, so nothing is granted on it", who="owner")
    hard = hard_lines(a, unread(t))
    move = credential_move(a, t)
    if move == "widen":
        return done("REFUSE", "a copy that widens who can read a credential (a member, anything public, a log); "
                    "perms refuses it")
    if move == "box":
        # never a grant: perms weighs it, and the owner is not asked (owner, 10-12)
        return done("ASK-OWNER", "a credential the box already holds, moved between its own services: perms' call, "
                    "not the owner's, so perms decides")
    if hard:
        return done("ASK-OWNER", *[f"hard line: {h}, on {w!r}; perms or the owner decides" for h, w in hard],
                    who="owner")
    shape = parse_shape(a.get("ask"))
    if not shape:
        return done("ASK-OWNER", "not one of the command shapes the box may grant itself; perms decides")
    out["shape"] = shape[0]
    good, bad = check_evidence(a.get("evidence"), a.get("ask"), cited_ok)
    out["evidence"], out["evidence_refused"] = good, bad
    if not good:
        return done("ASK-OWNER", "no resolved evidence of his intent for this ask, so perms decides")
    if shape[0] == "service":
        state = unit_state(shape[1])
        if state != "active":
            return done("ASK-OWNER", f"{shape[1]} is {state} now, so a restart would start it and its undo would be a "
                        "stop, a hard line; perms decides" if state else
                        f"{shape[1]}'s state can't be read, so a restart might start it; perms decides")
    out["revert"], out["revert_note"] = shape_undo(shape, a.get("revert"))   # after evidence: cc-config may take 20 s
    # a shape stays in the box and undoes in minutes; a claim can only make it stricter
    reach = a.get("reaches") if REACH_RANK.get(a.get("reaches"), 0) > 0 else "box"
    rev = a.get("reversible") if UNDO_RANK.get(a.get("reversible"), 0) > 0 else "minutes"
    out["reaches"], out["reversible"] = reach, rev
    if REACH_RANK[reach] > REACH_RANK["owner"]:
        return done("ASK-OWNER", f"it is said to reach {reach}, further than the box grants itself", who="owner")
    if rev == "no":
        return done("ASK-OWNER", "it is said to be impossible to undo")
    if rev == "minutes":
        return done("GRANT", f"a {shape[0]} shape with evidenced intent, in the box and undone in minutes")
    out["watch"] = {"check": squash(a.get("check")) or "probe that it still matches the goal", "revert": out["revert"],
                    "revert_note": out["revert_note"]}
    return done("GRANT+WATCH", f"a {shape[0]} shape with evidenced intent, said to take hours to undo, so it is watched")


def record(a, d):
    """The ledger line and, for GRANT+WATCH, the watcher registration in the spool."""
    if d["verdict"] not in GRANTS:
        return None
    sd, now = state_dir(), time.time()
    gid = "g" + time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%S", time.gmtime(now)) + f"-{os.getpid()}"
    os.makedirs(sd, exist_ok=True)
    line = {"id": gid, "at": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(now)), "verdict": d["verdict"],
            "what": d["ask"], "evidence": d["evidence"], "watcher": None, "revert": d.get("revert") or "",
            "revert_note": d.get("revert_note") or "",
            "from": str(a.get("from") or "")}
    if d["verdict"] == "GRANT+WATCH":
        os.makedirs(f"{sd}/watch-spool", exist_ok=True)
        reg = {"id": gid, "created": line["at"], "what": d["ask"], "check": d["watch"]["check"],
               "revert": d["watch"]["revert"], "revert_note": d["watch"]["revert_note"], "evidence": d["evidence"],
               "source": "cc-infer",
               "expires": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(now + WATCH_DAYS * 86400))}
        p = f"{sd}/watch-spool/{gid}.json"
        with open(p + ".tmp", "w") as f:
            json.dump(reg, f, ensure_ascii=False)
        os.replace(p + ".tmp", p)
        line["watcher"] = p
    with open(f"{sd}/inferred.jsonl", "a") as f:
        f.write(json.dumps(line, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    return line


def slack_safe(s):
    """Slack reads <...> as a mention or link (<!channel> pings everyone) and & as an entity: escape all three."""
    return str(s or "").replace("&", "&amp;").replace("<", "&lt;").replace(">", "&gt;")


def digest(hours=24):
    cut = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(time.time() - hours * 3600))
    rows = []
    try:
        for ln in open(f"{state_dir()}/inferred.jsonl", encoding="utf-8"):
            try:
                r = json.loads(ln)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if str(r.get("at") or "") > cut:   # both are whole-second stamps; the cut second itself is out
                rows.append(r)
    except OSError:
        return ""
    if not rows:
        return ""
    out = ["*Granted from your goals* (told after; nothing to tap)"]
    for r in rows[-6:]:
        src = ", ".join(e.get("source", "") for e in r.get("evidence") or []) or "?"
        out.append(f"• {slack_safe(str(r.get('what', ''))[:140])} (from {slack_safe(src[:60])}"
                   + (f"; undo: {slack_safe(r['revert'][:80])}" if r.get("revert")
                      else f"; {slack_safe(r['revert_note'][:100])}" if r.get("revert_note") else "") + ("; watched" if r.get("watcher") else "") + ")")
    if len(rows) > 6:
        out.append(f"• and {len(rows) - 6} more in {state_dir()}/inferred.jsonl.")
    return "\n".join(out)


# Rows the gate must keep with the owner. Perms ruling, 10-11: "Add negative rows from the record, one for each
# always-the-owner class ... Each of these rows must come back ASK-OWNER or REFUSE." owner-only marks such a row;
# perms-refused is a perms REFUSED entry.
BLOCKING = ("refused", "would-object", "perms-refused", "owner-only")


def backtest(path):
    """Replay past asks. The gate: no ask the owner refused or objected to may come out a GRANT."""
    rows, counts, bad, inferred = [], {}, [], 0
    for ln in open(path, encoding="utf-8"):
        if ln.strip():
            rows.append(json.loads(ln))
    for r in rows:
        a = {"ask": r.get("ask"), "kind": r.get("kind"), "reaches": r.get("reaches"), "reversible": r.get("reversible"),
             "money": r.get("money"), "data": r.get("data"), "via": r.get("via"), "port": r.get("port"),
             "evidence": [{"quote": r["goal_evidence"], "source": r.get("source") or "record"}] if r.get("goal_evidence") else []}
        d = decide(a, cited_ok=True)
        counts[d["verdict"]] = counts.get(d["verdict"], 0) + 1
        if d["verdict"] in GRANTS:
            inferred += 1
            if r.get("owner_outcome") in BLOCKING:
                bad.append((r.get("id"), r.get("owner_outcome"), d["verdict"], a["ask"]))
        print(f"{r.get('id', '?'):<14} {r.get('owner_outcome', '?'):<14} {d['verdict']:<12} {squash(a['ask'])[:90]}")
    print(f"\n{len(rows)} asks: " + ", ".join(f"{v} {counts[v]}" for v in ("GRANT", "GRANT+WATCH", "ASK-OWNER", "REFUSE") if v in counts)
          + f". {inferred} would have been inferred without him.")
    blocked = sum(1 for r in rows if r.get("owner_outcome") in BLOCKING)
    print(f"{blocked} he refused or objected to; {len(bad)} of them came out a grant.")
    for b in bad:
        print(f"  FALSE GRANT {b[0]} ({b[1]} -> {b[2]}): {b[3]}")
    return 1 if bad else 0


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["selfcheck"]:
        return selfcheck()
    if argv[:1] == ["digest"]:
        h = int(argv[2]) if argv[1:2] == ["--hours"] and len(argv) > 2 and argv[2].isdigit() else 24
        t = digest(h)
        if t:
            print(t)
        return 0
    if argv[:1] == ["backtest"] and len(argv) == 2:
        return backtest(argv[1])
    if argv[:1] != ["decide"]:
        print(USAGE, file=sys.stderr); return 2
    rest, rec = [x for x in argv[1:] if x != "--record"], "--record" in argv[1:]
    if len(rest) != 2 or rest[0] not in ("--json", "--ask"):
        print(USAGE, file=sys.stderr); return 2
    try:
        a = {"ask": rest[1]} if rest[0] == "--ask" else json.load(sys.stdin if rest[1] == "-" else open(rest[1]))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"cc-infer: can't read the ask: {e}", file=sys.stderr); return 2
    if not isinstance(a, dict):
        print("cc-infer: the ask must be one JSON object", file=sys.stderr); return 2
    d = decide(a)
    if rec:
        line = record(a, d)
        if line:
            d["ledger"] = line["id"]; d["watcher"] = line["watcher"]
    print(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False))
    return 0 if d["verdict"] in GRANTS else 1


def selfcheck():
    import contextlib, io, shutil, tempfile
    passed, failed = 0, []

    def check(name, ok):
        nonlocal passed
        if ok:
            passed += 1
        else:
            failed.append(name)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:
        _TEST.update(dir=f"{td}/perms", state=f"{td}/state", grants=f"{td}/host-rules.md", members=f"{td}/members",
                     repos=["proj"], config={}, systemctl=f"{td}/systemctl", never_touch=f"{td}/no-overlay/never-touch.txt")
        # a stand-in systemctl, so no real unit is ever read or touched: it logs its words and answers is-active from
        # units/<unit>, as the real one does (active exits 0, inactive 3, no bus 1 with nothing on stdout)
        os.makedirs(f"{td}/units")
        open(f"{td}/systemctl", "w").write(
            f'#!/bin/sh\nprintf "%s\\n" "$*" >> {td}/systemctl.log\n[ "$1 $2" = "--user is-active" ] || exit 64\n'
            f'read s < "{td}/units/$3" 2>/dev/null || s=inactive\n'
            'case "$s" in active) echo active; exit 0 ;; nobus) echo "Failed to connect to bus" >&2; exit 1 ;;\n'
            '  *) echo "$s"; exit 3 ;; esac\n')
        os.chmod(f"{td}/systemctl", 0o755)
        open(f"{td}/units/cc-slackd.service", "w").write("active\n")

        def unit(state):
            open(f"{td}/units/cc-slackd.service", "w").write(state + "\n")
        goals =f"{td}/state/proj/goals.md"
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(goals))
        # a stand-in Slack: SL holds the messages as Slack would serve them now, and every read is logged
        SL, slog = {}, []

        def say(ts, text, user="UOWNER", **kw):
            SL[("CPROJ", ts)] = dict(kw, ts=ts, text=text, **({"user": user} if user else {}))

        def fake_slack(method, channel, ts=None, latest=None, oldest=None, limit="100", **_):
            # as the real one does (probed 10-12): history is top-level only; replies for a reply's ts is that reply,
            # and for a parent's ts is the parent first and then up to `limit` replies from `oldest`, which the parent
            # doesn't count against
            slog.append((method, ts or latest, oldest, limit))
            here = {t: m for (c, t), m in SL.items() if c == channel}
            if method == "conversations.history":
                top = sorted(t for t, m in here.items() if m.get("thread_ts", t) == t and float(t) <= float(latest))
                return {"messages": [here[top[-1]]] if top else []}
            m = here.get(ts)
            if not m:
                raise RuntimeError("conversations.replies: thread_not_found")
            if m.get("thread_ts", ts) != ts:
                return {"messages": [m]}
            reps = sorted((x for t, x in here.items() if x.get("thread_ts") == ts and t != ts
                           and float(t) >= float(oldest or 0)), key=lambda x: float(x["ts"]))
            return {"messages": [m] + reps[:int(limit)]}
        _TEST.update(slack_api=fake_slack, slack_owner="UOWNER", owner_words=f"{td}/owner-words.jsonl")
        say("1728000000.000001", "Set cc-ask turns to 16.")
        say("1728000000.000002", "Restart cc-slackd.")
        say("1728000000.000003", "The proj repository is the one I care about most.")
        open(goals, "w").write("# Turns and daemons: proj standing goals (owner, 2026-08-31)\n"
                               "- Set cc-ask turns to 16. (src: slack:CPROJ/1728000000.000001)\n"
                               "- Restart cc-slackd. (src: slack:CPROJ/1728000000.000002)\n"
                               "- The proj repository is the one I care about most. (src: slack:CPROJ/1728000000.000003)\n"
                               "- more turns\n")
        ev = [{"quote": "Set cc-ask turns to 16.", "source": goals}]
        sev = [{"quote": "Restart cc-slackd.", "source": goals}]
        cfg = {"ask": "cc-config set CC_ASK_TURNS 16", "evidence": ev}
        svc = {"ask": "systemctl --user restart cc-slackd", "evidence": sev}
        # the closed set of shapes: each one, evidenced, is a GRANT; claimed hours to undo makes it watched
        for name, a in (("config", cfg), ("service", svc)):
            d = decide(a)
            check(f"the {name} shape with evidence is GRANT", d["verdict"] == "GRANT" and d["shape"] == name
                  and d["evidence"] and d["evidence"][0]["source"] == goals)
            d = decide(dict(a, reversible="hours"))
            check(f"... and GRANT+WATCH with the shape's own undo when it claims hours", d["verdict"] == "GRANT+WATCH"
                  and d["watch"]["revert"] == d["revert"])
            for claim in ({"reversible": "no"}, {"reaches": "member"}, {"reaches": "public"}):
                check(f"... and ASK-OWNER when it claims {claim}", decide(dict(a, **claim))["verdict"] == "ASK-OWNER")
            check(f"... and ASK-OWNER with no evidence", decide(dict(a, evidence=[]))["verdict"] == "ASK-OWNER")
            check(f"... and REFUSE once the owner refused it", decide(dict(a, owner_refused="T1"))["verdict"] == "REFUSE")
            check(f"... and ASK-OWNER under a hard kind", decide(dict(a, kind="controls"))["verdict"] == "ASK-OWNER")
        for k, (lo, hi) in CONFIG_KEYS.items():
            check(f"{k} parses at both ends of its range and not past them",
                  all(parse_shape(f"cc-config set {k} {v}") for v in (lo, hi))
                  and not any(parse_shape(f"cc-config set {k} {v}") for v in (lo - 1, hi + 1) if v >= 0))
        # anything that is not exactly a shape goes to perms, whatever the evidence
        for text in ("cc-config set CC_ASK_TURNS 99", "cc-config set CC_ASK_TURNS 0", "cc-config set CC_TIER 1",
